{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold code generation task (#5647) to extend the `cmd/ts` utility with four specific SRD requirements from srd004-ts:\n   - **R2.3**: Implement three ts-specific subsecond format extensions: `%.S` (seconds with microsecond suffix, e.g., \"32.001234\"), `%.s` (Unix epoch with microsecond suffix, e.g., \"1708358732.001234\"), `%.T` (HH:MM:SS with microsecond suffix, e.g., \"14:05:32.001234\"). Must format to six decimal places.\n   - **R2.4**: When subsecond extensions are used, obtain both second and microsecond components atomically from a single `time.Now()` call per line.\n   - **R3.1**: Implement `-i` (incremental) mode where the timestamp shows time elapsed since the previous line was received. The first line shows time elapsed since ts started.\n   - **R3.2**: In `-i` mode, the default format must be `\"%H:%M:%S\"` and TZ must be set to GMT internally so strftime on delta-second values produces correct elapsed strings.\n\n   Acceptance criteria require: `go build` compiles, `go test` passes including new tests, `go vet` clean, and at least one differential test per requirement.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Differential testing**: Compare Go binary output against moreutils `ts` reference binary using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - **strftime formatting**: Custom Go implementation of strftime with modifiers (`%-`, `%_`, `%0`)\n   - **Subsecond extensions**: ts-specific `%.S`, `%.s`, `%.T` format codes (dot-prefix notation)\n   - **Incremental time mode**: `-i` flag tracking elapsed time between consecutive stdin lines\n   - **TZ=GMT for elapsed modes**: Internal timezone override for delta-time formatting\n   - **TimestampNormalizer**: Test utility that replaces wall-clock timestamps with fixed placeholders for deterministic comparison\n   - **SIGPIPE handling**: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` required at start of main\n   - **Atomic time sampling**: Single `time.Now()` per line to avoid skew between second and subsecond components\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd004-ts.yaml**\n     - Full SRD defining all ts requirements R1-R10\n     - Critical for understanding the exact behavior of R2.3, R2.4, R3.1, R3.2\n     - R3.2 specifies: \"The default format in -i mode must be '%H:%M:%S'. The TZ environment must be set to GMT so that strftime on a delta-second value produces a correct elapsed string\"\n     - R3.4 (context): \"-i and -s are mutually exclusive; passing both must print a usage error to stderr and exit non-zero\"\n\n   - **cmd/ts/main.go** (existing implementation, 238 lines)\n     - Currently implements R1.1-R1.6, R2.1, R2.2 only\n     - Key functions that need modification:\n       ```go\n       const defaultFormat = \"%b %d %H:%M:%S\"\n       \n       func run() int {\n           format := parseFormat(os.Args[1:])\n           reader := bufio.NewReader(os.Stdin)\n           for {\n               line, err := reader.ReadString('\\n')\n               if len(line) > 0 {\n                   ts := formatTime(time.Now(), format)\n                   fmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"%s %s\", ts, line)\n               }\n               if err != nil {\n                   break\n               }\n           }\n           return 0\n       }\n       \n       func parseFormat(args []string) string {\n           for _, arg := range args {\n               if !strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"-\") {\n                   return arg\n               }\n           }\n           return defaultFormat\n       }\n       \n       func formatTime(t time.Time, format string) string {\n           // strftime implementation - handles %X specifiers with modifiers\n           // Does NOT handle %.X (dot-pre